exit: 0
--- stdout
commandments layers — Read the dependency stack this project ALREADY has and propose the layer declaration for it — the rule is inert until one is declared, and nobody writes that from a blank file.

Usage:
  commandments layers [path]        propose today's shape: every namespace with what it already uses
  commandments layers [path] --floor
                                    propose only the bottom — what others depend on and that
                                    depends on nothing
  commandments layers [path] --write
                                    add the proposal to .commandments/config.php
  commandments layers add <Namespace> [--may-use=A,B]
                                    declare a new layer, or widen a declared one, in place
  commandments layers allow <Layer> <Target>
                                    one more arrow, in place

Options:
  --floor        propose only the bottom layer
  --write        write the proposal into .commandments/config.php
  --refresh      with --write, regenerate a block that is already declared
  --may-use=A,B  with `add`, the namespaces the new layer may depend on

  Once a stack is declared the proposal refuses to overwrite it — a GROWING codebase edits it
  INCREMENTALLY with `add`/`allow`, or regenerates the whole block from today's shape with `--write
  --refresh`. Every edit goes through the AST and replaces only the ->layer(...) chain, keeping your
  config's own formatting.

